I'm an ex-Angbander and one thing it's taken me a while to get used to
in NH is how much more identifying things is a part of the game.  In
the *bands, ID is just a function of money because you can always go
back to town and get scrolls/wands/rods of ID.  In NH I sometimes
might have only found a couple scrolls of ID by the time I'm done with
Mines' End and Sokoban.  Sure, you can bless them (assuming you find/
convert an altar ;-) but often I have lots of stuff that hasn't been
formally ID'd.

Scrolls, potions, and wands can be ID'd if you know the tricks, and
with an altar anything wearable can be tried.  But what about gems?  I
know there's the unicorn trick, but shopkeepers won't pay you based on
the fact that a unicorn was grateful vs. gracious.

I seem to often find myself in Minetown with a sackload of gems and
wanting to buy divine protection, but with no way of getting my gems
ID'd...



